t(40, 1330, """In the event of the collapse of the global financial system and of paper currencies because of a total war, gold will immediately return to be the only real and accepted global currency for trade in strategic goods such as oil.

History and economic logic prove that gold is humanity's last refuge when trust in paper money disappears!

1. Gold has an "intrinsic value" that does not die

Paper currencies (such as the dollar or the euro) and digital currencies rely only on "trust" in the governments that print them. If these governments collapse or war destroys their economies, these papers become worthless. As for gold, it is a rare and precious metal with a fixed value that humans have recognised for thousands of years, and no government can print it or counterfeit it from nothing.

🛢️ 2. The Western states' need for oil will force them to pay with their gold

The states with the largest gold reserves in the world (such as America, Germany, Italy and France) are consumers of oil and gas. In contrast, the states that possess oil (such as the Gulf states and Iraq) will need it to build their economies and protect their wealth. The oil states will not accept any collapsed paper money, and the consuming states will be forced to open their treasuries and ship real gold ingots across the seas for every barrel of oil they obtain.

📜 3. Historical precedents that actually happened

This scenario is not imaginary; rather, things resembling it happened in less harsh conditions:

During the Second World War: Britain and European states were paying America pure gold to buy fuel and weapons, because their currencies were collapsing because of the war.

The sanctions on Iran and Venezuela: In recent years, when some states were isolated from the global banking system, states such as Venezuela paid with real gold ingots flown by aircraft to other states in exchange for obtaining their needs.

⚖️ 4. How will the price be assessed then?

The price of oil will not be measured in dollars (for example 70 dollars a barrel); rather, the world will return to the method of weight for weight. A clear equation will be agreed upon, such as: "Every 100 barrels of oil equal a specific quantity of grams of pure gold".""")

